"""Lead fixtures for the Leads page, generated by the REAL backend (voice-agent/leads.py).

Run from katie-dashboard/:

    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ../voice-agent/.venv/bin/python scripts/leads-fixtures.py

It imports voice-agent/leads.py read-only and points it at a throwaway database in the system
temp folder (LEADS_DB_PATH), plays one made-up practice's leads through the backend's own hooks
(quote sent, Katie's booking, a text cancel, the clock sweep, the PMS check-in, the coordinator's
taps, STOP), and writes what the dashboard routes would answer:

    src/mock/fixtures/leads.json        the store as of the fixtures' "now" (status.json: Monday
                                        2026-10-12 18:05:40 America/New_York)   -> ?mock=1
    src/mock/fixtures/leads-week.json   the same story as of 21:10 on each weekday of that week
                                        (Mon..Sun), so the demo day and the fake API can show it
                                        on today's date with the right weekdays (whole-week shift,
                                        src/mock/leadStore.ts seedForDate)        -> ?mock=demo
    scripts/fixtures/leads-actions.json what the backend answers to every coordinator tap on every
                                        fixture lead (and a few two-step chains), plus each
                                        filter's rows. scripts/check-lib.mjs replays them through
                                        the mock (src/mock/leadStore.ts) and fails on a difference.

Every name, number, appointment id and dollar figure is invented. Phones end 555-01xx (the
reserved fictional range) and leave this script masked, as the list route sends them.
Nothing in voice-agent/ is written: no bytecode (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE), no database, no log.
"""
